{% if part == "Vars" %}
{% endif %}
{% if part == "Doc" %}	DONE:
	- added the meta data from the real book.
	- put in the tunes structure.
	- put in the chords (real book).
	- put in the tune (real book).
	- added youtube performances (the real book refers to Gary Burton and Steve Swallow - 'Hotel Hello').
	TODO:
	- check the chords (real book).
	- check the tune (real book).
	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the book prints three staves: chord symbols with slashes marked 'Solo:', chord voicings in dotted half notes (bars 3 and 4 add a second chord in parentheses marked '1 X only'), and a bass line. The voice here is the bass line; the voicings are not typed (the chord symbols give the harmony).
	- the chord symbols of bars 7-9 and 10 are drawn as a circled letter without a clear flat (maj7 #11 and maj7); they are read as Gb (as in bar 5) but could be D or G. Check against the voicings and a recording.
	- the intro bars have no chord symbol; Db is taken from the voicing.
	REMARKS:
	- the book marks 'Fine' at the end of bar 4 and 'Last x ritard' under bars 3-4.
{% endif %}
{% if part == "ChordsReal" %}\chordmode {
	\startChords
	\startSong

	\myMark "Intro"
	\startPart
	des2. | des2. | \myEndLine
	\endPart

	\myMark "A"
	\startPart
	\repeat volta 2 {
		des2. | des2. | \myEndLine
		ges2.:maj7 | ges:maj7 | ges:maj7.11+ | ges:maj7.11+ | \myEndLine
		ges2.:maj7.11+ | ges:maj7 | des | aes:7 | \myEndLine
	}
	\endPart

	\endSong
	\endChords
}
{% endif %}
{% if part == "VoiceReal" %}{
	\tempo "Moderato" 4 = 120
	\time 3/4
	\key des \major

	% part "Intro"
	\clef bass
	r4 r4 ges4^\markup { Bass } | ges4. f8 ees4 |

	% part "A"
	\repeat volta 2 {
		f4. ees8 des4 | ees2.^\markup { \italic Fine } | r4 r4 f4 | f4. ees8 des4 | ees2. |
		ees4. f8 ges4 | ges4. f8 ees4 | ees2. | f4. ees8 des4 | ees4. f8 ges4 |
	}
}
{% endif %}
